2026-09-12 08:18:05 EDT [CRAWLER] MANASSAS, Va., Sept. 12, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Meant Health, a digital health platform that connects patients with licensed clinicians for evaluation, prescription and ongoing care coaching, announced today that it is expanding telehealth access to FDA-approved GLP-1 medications. The move is meant to shorten the distance between someone wondering whether a treatment might be right for them and an actual conversation with a U.S.-licensed clinician who could review their history and make that call.
2026-09-12 08:18:05 EDT [CRAWLER] How the Evaluation and Prescription Process Works
2026-09-12 08:18:05 EDT [CRAWLER] As more people look for a straightforward way to access Ozempic, Meant Health is expanding its telehealth platform to connect patients with licensed clinicians for evaluation and prescription. It starts with an intake questionnaire that walks through health history, current medications and what the patient is hoping to address. A licensed clinician then reviews that information and decides, case by case, whether a prescription makes sense.
