2026-09-12 08:18:06 EDT [CRAWLER] Now available via early access: image-based search retrieves real, diagnosed reference cases from world-class centers, spanning 300+ diagnostic entities.
2026-09-12 08:18:06 EDT [CRAWLER] BERLIN and NEW YORK, Sept. 12, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Today, Aignostics announced the early access release of PathoSearch, a visual search engine for pathology cases. From a single screenshot of a region of interest on an H&E slide, PathoSearch instantly retrieves morphologically similar, diagnosed reference cases. Pathologists can then build and evaluate a differential in minutes — especially useful on the rare and complex cases that are hardest to resolve.
2026-09-12 08:18:06 EDT [CRAWLER] These cases account for up to 20% of a pathologist's caseload, and the current references available for them are largely what they have always been: textbooks, databases, or external consultations. Each of these options adds time and cost for pathologists, with consultation fees at major cancer centers running from several hundred to thousands of dollars per case.
