2026-09-12 08:18:09 EDT [CRAWLER] On September 9, Caleres (NYSE:CAL) held its second-quarter earnings call, and the numbers told two very different stories under one roof. Net sales rose 5.6% to $695.5 million, and adjusted diluted earnings per share jumped to $0.47 from $0.35 a year earlier. The company also raised the low end of its full-year guidance. Yet Famous Footwear, the chain that made Caleres a household name, kept losing ground while the newer brand portfolio did the heavy lifting.  
